Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.950
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.950
#Wasurenai@irc.rizon.net

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:48.310
Good morning. Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.190
That is so nice. I want to be like Tennouji-san too.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.670
I want to work in this shop!

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.170
They will never hire a beginner, right?

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.330
In the first place, it's impossible for a student from middle school division.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.690
It's not impossible!

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.920
Even for me, I should be able to become a waitress in there.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.620
Even if being a waitress, you must be a student of the high school division.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.270
N-No way...

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:13.330
I really wanted to try working in this store, too.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.790
If it's for that, I know just the right shop.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.780
Really?

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.840
Where is it?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.320
Andou's house is a Japanese confectionery.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.580
Really, is that so?

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.470
Yeah. I always go back on weekends to help out at the shop.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:32.210
I'll be there to make snacks tomorrow. Would you like to come too, Ichigo-chan?

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.720
Hanabusa, don't say anything unnecessary-

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.830
Really? May I come along too?

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.650
Of course. Please come along and help out, Amano-san.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.860
Yippee! Amano Ichigo will do her best!

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:48.870
recipe 4

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:48.870
I Hate Cakes<i>!</i>

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:54.580
Yume

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:54.580
Tsuki

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.990
Thank you for waiting. Here's your dango set.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.580
Onee-san. This table wants green tea and zenzai.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.790
Zenzai=snack commonly served at weddings

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:55.790
Yes, right away.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.290
Hey, where's my water?

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.000
Yes, right away.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.570
Thank you for waiting, here's your mame kan.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.720
Welcome! Sorry to make you wait.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.720
Phew, there are so many things a waitress has to do. It's really difficult to be one.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.510
What, are you tired already?

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.370
That's not true.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.230
Then, what's the order?

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.630
Err... what was it again?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:22.830
One zenzai and three shiratama kintoki.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.150
Shiratama kintoki=a kind of sweet bean dumpling snack

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.150
Thank you, Vanilla.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.950
What are you whispering about?

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.940
Umm... One zenzai and three shiratama kintoki.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.800
Onee-tan, let's play.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.560
Sorry, but I'm still working.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.510
Somehow... they...

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:39.720
Let's play!

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.670
Hey, Chiho, Marie, Momoe.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.260
You must behave yourselves.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.890
I'm sorry, Amano-san.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.890
No, it's alright.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.160
Geez, these kids.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.460
Mamo-nii-tan.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.160
Oh, Mamo?

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.790
Kashino and I are childhood friends.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.070
I see. So that's why the kids are familiar with him, too.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.610
Now, you guys go play at the back of the house, okay?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.090
What a big family.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.190
It's a rare scene even in the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.000
Yes, I think he has another younger brother too.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.500
Hey, cake pig.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.190
Oh my, you're the younger brother, Ichita-kun, right?

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.690
Who are you calling a cake pig!?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:29.110
I am Ichigo. Ichigo-neesan! I am not a pig. <i>Not a pig</i>!

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.600
I heard from Ma-bou.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.990
Eh? What?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:35.110
That you're good at gobbling down cakes.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.900
That's why, you are a cake pig!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.920
What did you say?

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.700
Are you calling me a glutton? Feast your eyes on this!

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.170
Hey, what is that weird medal for?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.500
A cake pig will always be a cake pig.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.010
Don't say anymore!

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.510
This is a Japanese confectionery.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.020
We don't need a person who wants to open a cake shop here.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.300
Go home quickly!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.270
Why do you say that?

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.160
Isn't your brother working towards being a pâtissier too?

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:00.880
Nii-chan is...

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:02.930
Ichita-kun?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.300
What are you doing here?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:12.620
Never mind. Let's take a break. Ichita, come along.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.470
I got some cakes to give you as a present.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.660
I... hate cakes!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.300
Ichita.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.230
Ichita-kun.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.500
I made Ichita hate me.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.800
He's already in first grade, isn't he?

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.350
Then, could he be at a rebellious age?

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.740
Yeah, but...

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.830
We were so close before.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.750
But he hardly speaks to me now.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.180
Nii-chan's lonely.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.160
Why did he look so lonely?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.570
Ah... this mame daifuku is so soft.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:59.070
On top of that, the bean paste is surprisingly smooth and the red beans are fluffy and warm.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.730
It's like it's going to melt on my tongue.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.790
That's our best selling product.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.320
Delicious!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.390
If it's this, I can keep eating forever.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.430
Here you go.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.210
I thought I was going to die.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.080
No matter how you look at it, you're overeating, aren't you?

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:21.580
But grandpa would be pleased that you liked them so much.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.950
Did your grandpa make these?

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.210
That's right. Would you like to see where he makes them?

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:27.970
Yes!

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:33.750
I'm so happy. Did you like our daifuku that much?

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.750
Yes, they are extremely delicious.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.880
Umm... is that the sweet paste used to fill the mame daifuku?

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:40.970
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:43.810
Here. Try some.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.600
Thank you very much.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.030
It's sweet.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.160
As I thought, there is a secret formula for making this, right?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.360
Not really.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.510
We're just following the recipe that's been passed down from generation to generation.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.160
That is, attention to the basics.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.160
Attention to the basics...

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:06.240
Like keeping a close watch so the bean paste doesn't burn.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.880
Handling each process with care.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.630
And selecting each azuki individually.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.580
Those are the basics for Japanese confectionery.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.310
After that, we hope that the person who eats it will be pleased.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.760
We keep all this in mind throughout the process.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.470
If you've to say it, that could be the secret formula.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:24.120
With hopes that the person who eats it will be pleased.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:24.880
I see.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:30.900
The smiles on the customers at the shop hold the taste of happiness that's been passed through the generations.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:33.760
Well, something like that.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.190
Acting like an expert when it's only at the mouth.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:41.790
That was what grandpa had understood. But when I make cakes, I hold those feelings too.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.790
Say, why are you aiming to be a pâtissier when your family runs a Japanese confectionery?

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.960
Because when I was little, during a birthday party at Kashino's house...

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.180
Delicious!

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:58.680
What is this?

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.450
Haven't you ever eaten a cake before?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.930
Nope. I've never had anything like this.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.130
Delicious! It's really delicious!

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:13.320
The first cake I had was beautiful, sweet and melted in my mouth.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.900
That taste was completely different from Japanese confectionery.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:21.440
After that, every day I pestered my father to make cakes for me.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:23.120
Daddy, cake, cake!

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.830
Then I tried making it myself one day.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:30.860
Using the bean paste from home, I made a Maccha Roll Cake.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:32.390
It was really delicious.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.820
That was when I decided.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:38.470
I was going to make sweets of Japanese and Western combinations that inherit from the Yumetsuki tradition.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.550
For that dream, I must obtain the skill for making cakes as well.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:44.660
And maybe one day, I will start my shop next door.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:49.490
I see. Andou-kun's dreams took shape in this house, too.

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.200
Are you still here, cake pig?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.250
Didn't I say cake bakers should go away?

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.010
Geez, why you...

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:11.620
Hey, Ichita. We finally got a helper.
Why are you speaking to her like that?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.810
That hurts. We don't need a cake baker here.

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:17.760
Ichita-kun. Does that apply to Onii-san as well?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.430
Well, that's...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.670
Ah... there's that expression again.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:25.830
Anyway, I hate cakes!

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.240
Go back to your homes now!

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:29.870
Ichita-kun!

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.940
Cake Pig, Mapo Tofu, Narcissistic!

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.270
Narcissistic...

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:35.590
Mapo tofu!

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:40.300
Don't laugh. That brat!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:40.660
Wait.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.570
He must have a reason for hating cakes.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.410
I'll go check it out.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.270
Hold on. Let's not meddle!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:15.780
There he is.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.780
Hey... that looks good, doesn't it?

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.480
W-Why did you come in here, cake pig?

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.090
Ichigo-oneesan.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:44.300
I've seen your grandpa making that. It's bean paste, right?

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.470
Y-Yeah.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.400
I'm practicing.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:54.480
Not just selecting the azuki beans, but also making the paste properly.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.690
These are the azuki beans used to make bean paste.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.700
So, you remove the worm eaten ones.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.410
Grandpa and the others have bad eyesight.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.100
That's my job.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.260
I see.

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:20.340
With all the effort Ichita-kun puts in, they should turn out delicious.

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.060
Hey, of course.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:24.880
The method for selecting azuki beans has been passed down for over a thousand years.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.290
The method of making the bean paste as well.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:30.230
It'll be done soon.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:32.470
Ichita-kun looks so happy.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:37.820
While he says that he hates cakes, he must love Andou-kun after all.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:44.320
If Ichita-kun comes to like cakes too, his feelings for Andou-kun may grow deeper.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:45.840
All right!

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.050
Say, Ichita-kun.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.170
Please wait here.

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.040
I'll bring you something nice.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.470
Why... did you bring cakes?

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.630
These are not just cakes.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:09.260
These are especially delicious cakes from Salon de Marie in our school.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:12.980
It'll be alright!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.730
I told you I hate cakes, right?

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.730
Just one mouthful is fine. Try eating it.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.230
Stop that already.

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:20.230
How about one with strawberry mousse?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.540
I said I don't want any!

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:23.640
The cake is...

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:24.740
Ichita!

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.370
Andou-kun.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.360
What are you doing to the food?

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.030
Even so, you still dare call yourself a confectioner's son?

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:32.880
This is a Japanese confectionery, right?

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.400
Cakes don't matter!

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:39.710
Nii-chan does prefer cakes after all.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.830
Sen-nii and cakes. I hate you!

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:45.790
Ichita-kun!

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.190
I'm sorry for forcing you to eat.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.880
Do you really hate cakes that much?

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.220
But you don't hate your Onii-chan, right?

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:38.180
Sen-nii is... Why does Sen-nii have to go to a cake school?

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.590
The method of selecting azuki, and even making bean paste...

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.200
Sen-nii will teach me everything, right?

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:05.620
It was my dream to make snacks with my talented Sen-nii at our shop.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:06.370
And yet...

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:14.800
And yet, Sen-nii... abandoned our home to be a cake baker.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.360
He chose cakes over me.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.740
I hate cakes which stole away my dreams!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.750
Ichita-kun doesn't know of Andou-kun's dreams...

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:35.250
I see, how Ichita-kun behaved earlier was like...

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.500
how I used to behave.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.560
Don't cry.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.340
Not too long ago, both you and I were alike, you know.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:51.000
I was chasing after my sister who is good at piano.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:55.760
I couldn't see my own dreams at all and had always felt lonely.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:58.860
Ichigo, you too?

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:02.180
But I can see my dreams clearly now.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:06.190
So, Ichita-kun will definitely find a new dream, too.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.070
But, Sen-nii is no longer at home...

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.450
That's fine.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:17.520
I'll tell you about Onii-chan's dreams and how he truly feels.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:19.010
I see.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.320
Ichita had such misconceptions.

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:26.670
Since your parents are busy with the shop, the kids must be lonely.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.720
Yes, I might have made the wrong choice.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:33.240
Hey, then let's make Ichita-kun some cakes.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:34.930
Wouldn't that have the opposite effect?

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:40.020
No. If Andou-kun makes the cake he truly wants to, he'll eat it.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:43.100
A cake that I truly want to make?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.120
Yes.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:27.330
Finally, we just have to add this and it's complete.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:28.510
That is...

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.610
I wonder if this would please Ichita-kun.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.340
I'm sure it will.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.470
We'll need to prepare the plates.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.140
Oui. This feels good.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.140
Even though it's not made by Ichigo, I'll include this too.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:17:59.460
We're ready.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:01.530
Come along now.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.060
Stop shoving me already...

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.000
Onii-tan.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:13.000
S-Sen-nii.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.810
Huh... what's in that box?

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:19.660
We wanted you to try this, so we made it together.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.900
Did you make some daifuku?

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:23.720
No, this is slightly different.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.080
This is a really delicious roll cake.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:34.530
If remember correctly, it should be the cake Sennosuke made when he was around your age, Ichita.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.780
Eh? Sen-nii did?

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:37.960
Ichita, come and try it.

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.120
B-But, I hate cakes.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:48.190
Ichita-kun. I said I'd tell you your Onii-chan's true feelings, right?

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:50.600
This cake's one of them.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.560
Here.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:56.420
Sen-nii's true feelings.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.810
I get it.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.060
But just one bite, that's all.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:14.360
Delicious!!

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.080
Really, it's delicious.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.540
This is definitely delicious.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.300
You're right. But there's a subtle difference in our bean paste.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:25.010
Ichita made that bean paste.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:26.470
Mine?

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.850
In short, that's the brothers' Maccha Roll Cake.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.580
Brothers' Maccha Roll Cake.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:39.070
Andou-kun's cake and Ichita-kun's bean paste make a dreamy collaboration.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.250
That was my idea.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:43.550
You didn't do most of the work though.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:50.790
The snacks that Sen-nii wants to make are combinations of Japanese confectionery and cakes, like this?

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:52.170
That's right.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.320
My roots are, after all, Japanese confectionery from Yumetsuki.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:59.340
Someday, I'll definitely start a new shop next door, using the name Yumetsuki.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:01.370
That is my dream.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.270
I will definitely not give that up.

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:06.170
Yumetsuki will expand in my hands.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.900
Sen-nii.

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.790
I'm sorry for making you worry, Ichita.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.480
Sen-nii!

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.150
That's great, Ichita-kun.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.830
Thank you for everything.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.210
Do come to play again.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:32.860
Yes.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.640
Wait up, cake pig.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.050
You're still calling me that!

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:43.000
I found my dream.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:48.560
If Nii-chan is starting a shop next door, I'll take over this one.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.270
That is a wonderful dream.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:54.210
Just you wait. I'll soon exceed a beginner like you.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:55.580
Ichita.

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:58.280
You and I are rivals starting today.

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:02.820
Hold it. I don't want to be called a rival by a grade schooler.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:04.740
Do you lack confidence, cake pig?

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.290
Ah, you said it again!

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:07.450
Unforgivable!

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:09.910
That's different.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:09.910
Glutton indeed.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:11.650
Catch me if you can.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:14.210
She's definitely more like a grade schooler.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.250
Stop running you coward!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.060
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

